-- ca-interpretation-repeal.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: what a repeal does (sections 2(2), 39(2), 42 to 46).
-- Where the text answers by a rule that turns on a fact the caller knows, the fact is an input.
-- Where the text names some things and the caller asks about another, the answer is a named refusal.

§ `Section 2(2): an enactment that is replaced or has ceased to have effect`

-- "an enactment that has been replaced is repealed and an enactment that has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect is
-- deemed to have been repealed".  An enactment that is none of these three is not said by this subsection to be anything.
-- src:25 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, an enactment that has been replaced is repealed and an enactment that has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect is deemed to have been repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(2) (src:25)
GIVEN `it has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`for the purposes of the Act, an enactment is treated as repealed if` `it has been repealed` `or` `it has been replaced` `or` `it has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect` MEANS
        `it has been repealed`
     OR `it has been replaced`
     OR `it has expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect`

§ `Section 39(2): a regulation annulled by a resolution`

-- "it is deemed to have been revoked on the day the resolution is passed and any law that was revoked or amended by the making of
-- that regulation is deemed to be revived on the day the resolution is passed".
-- Before the day of the resolution the regulation is in force; after it, it is revoked and the law it revoked or amended is revived.
-- On the day of the resolution itself the text gives the day and not the moment: section 6(1) fixes the moment of a day named by an
-- enactment "expressed to" expire, which a revocation deemed by section 39(2) is not.  The answer for that day is a refusal (fork F-39-2-MOMENT).
-- src:381 | (2) Where a regulation is annulled by a resolution of Parliament or of the House of Commons, it is deemed to have been revoked on the day the resolution is passed and any law that was revoked or amended by the making of that regulation is deemed to be revived on the day the resolution is passed, but the validity of any action taken or not taken in compliance with a regulation so deemed to have been revoked shall not be affected by the resolution.
@ref Interpretation Act s 39(2) (src:381)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` `the day the resolution is passed` `is in force on` e MEANS
    IF   e LESS THAN `the day the resolution is passed`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF   e GREATER THAN `the day the resolution is passed`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE `the Act gives the day on which an annulled regulation is revoked and a revived law revived and not the moment within that day`

-- src:381 | (2) Where a regulation is annulled by a resolution of Parliament or of the House of Commons, it is deemed to have been revoked on the day the resolution is passed and any law that was revoked or amended by the making of that regulation is deemed to be revived on the day the resolution is passed, but the validity of any action taken or not taken in compliance with a regulation so deemed to have been revoked shall not be affected by the resolution.
@ref Interpretation Act s 39(2) (src:381)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a law revoked or amended by the making of a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` `the day the resolution is passed` `is in force in its earlier form on` e MEANS
    IF   e LESS THAN `the day the resolution is passed`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF   e GREATER THAN `the day the resolution is passed`
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE `the Act gives the day on which an annulled regulation is revoked and a revived law revived and not the moment within that day`

-- src:381 | (2) Where a regulation is annulled by a resolution of Parliament or of the House of Commons, it is deemed to have been revoked on the day the resolution is passed and any law that was revoked or amended by the making of that regulation is deemed to be revived on the day the resolution is passed, but the validity of any action taken or not taken in compliance with a regulation so deemed to have been revoked shall not be affected by the resolution.
@ref Interpretation Act s 39(2) (src:381): the moment within the day is not given
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Act gives the day on which an annulled regulation is revoked and a revived law revived and not the moment within that day` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Act gives the day on which an annulled regulation is revoked and a revived law revived and not the moment within that day"

-- "the validity of any action taken or not taken in compliance with a regulation so deemed to have been revoked shall not be
-- affected by the resolution": the validity is whatever it was.
-- src:381 | (2) Where a regulation is annulled by a resolution of Parliament or of the House of Commons, it is deemed to have been revoked on the day the resolution is passed and any law that was revoked or amended by the making of that regulation is deemed to be revived on the day the resolution is passed, but the validity of any action taken or not taken in compliance with a regulation so deemed to have been revoked shall not be affected by the resolution.
@ref Interpretation Act s 39(2) (src:381)
GIVEN `the action was valid before the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an action taken or not taken in compliance with the annulled regulation is valid after the resolution if it was` `the action was valid before the resolution` MEANS
    `the action was valid before the resolution`

§ `Section 43: effect of repeal`

DECLARE `A thing a repeal is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `an enactment, or anything, not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect`
    `the previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it`
    `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment`
    `an offence against, or a contravention of the provisions of, the repealed enactment`
    `a punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the repealed enactment`
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability, or of such a punishment, penalty or forfeiture`
    `anything else`

DECLARE `What section 43 says a repeal does to it` IS ONE OF
    `the repeal does not revive it`
    `the repeal does not affect it`

-- src:409 | 43 Where an enactment is repealed in whole or in part, the repeal does not
-- src:410 | (a) revive any enactment or anything not in force or existing at the time when the repeal takes effect,
-- src:411 | (b) affect the previous operation of the enactment so repealed or anything duly done or suffered thereunder,
-- src:412 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the enactment so repealed,
-- src:413 | (d) affect any offence committed against or contravention of the provisions of the enactment so repealed, or any punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the enactment so repealed, or
-- src:414 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any right, privilege, obligation or liability referred to in paragraph (c) or in respect of any punishment, penalty or forfeiture referred to in paragraph (d),
@ref Interpretation Act s 43 (src:409-414)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing a repeal is asked about`
GIVETH A `What section 43 says a repeal does to it`
`what section 43 says the repeal does to` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `an enactment, or anything, not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` THEN `the repeal does not revive it`
    WHEN `the previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it` THEN `the repeal does not affect it`
    WHEN `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` THEN `the repeal does not affect it`
    WHEN `an offence against, or a contravention of the provisions of, the repealed enactment` THEN `the repeal does not affect it`
    WHEN `a punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the repealed enactment` THEN `the repeal does not affect it`
    WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability, or of such a punishment, penalty or forfeiture` THEN `the repeal does not affect it`
    WHEN `anything else` THEN `section 43 names five things a repeal does not revive or affect and does not say what a repeal does to anything else`

-- src:409 | 43 Where an enactment is repealed in whole or in part, the repeal does not
-- src:410 | (a) revive any enactment or anything not in force or existing at the time when the repeal takes effect,
-- src:411 | (b) affect the previous operation of the enactment so repealed or anything duly done or suffered thereunder,
-- src:412 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the enactment so repealed,
-- src:413 | (d) affect any offence committed against or contravention of the provisions of the enactment so repealed, or any punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the enactment so repealed, or
-- src:414 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any right, privilege, obligation or liability referred to in paragraph (c) or in respect of any punishment, penalty or forfeiture referred to in paragraph (d),
-- src:415 | and an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy as described in paragraph (e) may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the punishment, penalty or forfeiture may be imposed as if the enactment had not been so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act s 43 (src:409-415): the five paragraphs name five things; nothing else is named
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 43 names five things a repeal does not revive or affect and does not say what a repeal does to anything else` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 43 names five things a repeal does not revive or affect and does not say what a repeal does to anything else"

-- The closing words: "an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy as described in paragraph (e) may be instituted, continued or
-- enforced, and the punishment, penalty or forfeiture may be imposed as if the enactment had not been so repealed".
-- src:415 | and an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy as described in paragraph (e) may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the punishment, penalty or forfeiture may be imposed as if the enactment had not been so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act s 43 (src:415)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing a repeal is asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability, or of such a punishment, penalty or forfeiture` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the repealed enactment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enactment, or anything, not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` THEN `the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only`
    WHEN `the previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it` THEN `the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only`
    WHEN `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` THEN `the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only`
    WHEN `an offence against, or a contravention of the provisions of, the repealed enactment` THEN `the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only`
    WHEN `anything else` THEN `the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only`

-- src:415 | and an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy as described in paragraph (e) may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the punishment, penalty or forfeiture may be imposed as if the enactment had not been so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act s 43 (src:415)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only` MEANS
    REFUSE "the closing words of section 43 speak of an investigation, proceeding or remedy and of a punishment, penalty or forfeiture only"

§ `Section 44: repeal and substitution`

-- (a) every person acting under the former enactment shall continue to act, as if appointed under the new enactment, until another
-- person is appointed in the stead of that person.
-- src:418 | (a) every person acting under the former enactment shall continue to act, as if appointed under the new enactment, until another person is appointed in the stead of that person;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(a) (src:418)
GIVEN `another person has been appointed in the stead of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person who was acting under the former enactment continues to act under the new enactment if` `another person has been appointed in the stead of that person` MEANS
    NOT `another person has been appointed in the stead of that person`

-- (b) every bond and security given by a person appointed under the former enactment remains in force; all books, papers, forms and
-- things made or used under it continue to be used as before the repeal in so far as they are consistent with the new enactment.
-- src:419 | (b) every bond and security given by a person appointed under the former enactment remains in force, and all books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment shall continue to be used as before the repeal in so far as they are consistent with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(b) (src:419)
GIVEN `the bond or security was given by a person appointed under the former enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a bond or security remains in force if` `the bond or security was given by a person appointed under the former enactment` MEANS
    IF   `the bond or security was given by a person appointed under the former enactment`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 44(b) speaks of a bond or security given by a person appointed under the former enactment and of nothing else`

-- src:419 | (b) every bond and security given by a person appointed under the former enactment remains in force, and all books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment shall continue to be used as before the repeal in so far as they are consistent with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(b) (src:419)
GIVEN `it is consistent with the new enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment continue to be used as before the repeal if` `it is consistent with the new enactment` MEANS
    IF   `it is consistent with the new enactment`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 44(b) says they continue to be used so far as consistent and does not say what happens to those that are not`

-- src:419 | (b) every bond and security given by a person appointed under the former enactment remains in force, and all books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment shall continue to be used as before the repeal in so far as they are consistent with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(b) (src:419): the negative case is not stated
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(b) speaks of a bond or security given by a person appointed under the former enactment and of nothing else` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(b) speaks of a bond or security given by a person appointed under the former enactment and of nothing else"

-- src:419 | (b) every bond and security given by a person appointed under the former enactment remains in force, and all books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment shall continue to be used as before the repeal in so far as they are consistent with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(b) (src:419): the negative case is not stated
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(b) says they continue to be used so far as consistent and does not say what happens to those that are not` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(b) says they continue to be used so far as consistent and does not say what happens to those that are not"

-- (c) every proceeding taken under the former enactment shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with the new
-- enactment in so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment.
-- src:420 | (c) every proceeding taken under the former enactment shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with the new enactment in so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(c) (src:420)
GIVEN `it may be done consistently with the new enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proceeding taken under the former enactment is taken up and continued under the new enactment if` `it may be done consistently with the new enactment` MEANS
    IF   `it may be done consistently with the new enactment`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 44(c) says a proceeding is continued so far as that may be done consistently and does not say what happens to one that cannot`

-- src:420 | (c) every proceeding taken under the former enactment shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with the new enactment in so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(c) (src:420): the negative case is not stated
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(c) says a proceeding is continued so far as that may be done consistently and does not say what happens to one that cannot` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(c) says a proceeding is continued so far as that may be done consistently and does not say what happens to one that cannot"

-- (d) the procedure established by the new enactment shall be followed as far as it can be adapted, in (i) the recovery or
-- enforcement of fines, penalties and forfeitures imposed under the former enactment, (ii) the enforcement of rights, existing or
-- accruing under the former enactment, and (iii) a proceeding in relation to matters that have happened before the repeal.
-- src:421 | (d) the procedure established by the new enactment shall be followed as far as it can be adapted thereto
-- src:422 | (i) in the recovery or enforcement of fines, penalties and forfeitures imposed under the former enactment,
-- src:423 | (ii) in the enforcement of rights, existing or accruing under the former enactment, and
-- src:424 | (iii) in a proceeding in relation to matters that have happened before the repeal;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(d) (src:421-424)
GIVEN `it can be adapted to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the procedure of the new enactment is followed in recovering fines, enforcing rights or proceeding on earlier matters if` `it can be adapted to the matter` MEANS
    IF   `it can be adapted to the matter`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 44(d) says the new procedure is followed as far as it can be adapted and does not say what procedure applies where it cannot`

-- src:421 | (d) the procedure established by the new enactment shall be followed as far as it can be adapted thereto
-- src:422 | (i) in the recovery or enforcement of fines, penalties and forfeitures imposed under the former enactment,
-- src:423 | (ii) in the enforcement of rights, existing or accruing under the former enactment, and
-- src:424 | (iii) in a proceeding in relation to matters that have happened before the repeal;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(d) (src:421-424): the negative case is not stated
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(d) says the new procedure is followed as far as it can be adapted and does not say what procedure applies where it cannot` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(d) says the new procedure is followed as far as it can be adapted and does not say what procedure applies where it cannot"

-- (e) when any punishment, penalty or forfeiture is reduced or mitigated by the new enactment, the punishment, penalty or forfeiture
-- if imposed or adjudged after the repeal shall be reduced or mitigated accordingly.
DECLARE `Which punishment applies` IS ONE OF
    `the punishment as reduced or mitigated by the new enactment`
    `the punishment under the former enactment`

-- src:425 | (e) when any punishment, penalty or forfeiture is reduced or mitigated by the new enactment, the punishment, penalty or forfeiture if imposed or adjudged after the repeal shall be reduced or mitigated accordingly;
-- src:413 | (d) affect any offence committed against or contravention of the provisions of the enactment so repealed, or any punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the enactment so repealed, or
-- src:414 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any right, privilege, obligation or liability referred to in paragraph (c) or in respect of any punishment, penalty or forfeiture referred to in paragraph (d),
-- src:415 | and an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy as described in paragraph (e) may be instituted, continued or enforced, and the punishment, penalty or forfeiture may be imposed as if the enactment had not been so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(e) (src:425) and s 43 (src:413-415)
GIVEN `the new enactment reduces or mitigates the punishment, penalty or forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed or adjudged after the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which punishment applies`
`the punishment, penalty or forfeiture that applies where` `the new enactment reduces or mitigates the punishment, penalty or forfeiture` `and` `it is imposed or adjudged after the repeal` MEANS
    IF       `the new enactment reduces or mitigates the punishment, penalty or forfeiture`
         AND `it is imposed or adjudged after the repeal`
    THEN `the punishment as reduced or mitigated by the new enactment`
    ELSE `the punishment under the former enactment`

-- (f) except to the extent that the provisions of the new enactment are not in substance the same as those of the former
-- enactment, the new enactment shall not be held to operate as new law, but shall be construed and have effect as a consolidation
-- and as declaratory of the law as contained in the former enactment.
DECLARE `How a provision of the new enactment is read` IS ONE OF
    `as a consolidation and as declaratory of the law in the former enactment`
    `as capable of operating as new law, to the extent that it is not in substance the same`

-- src:426 | (f) except to the extent that the provisions of the new enactment are not in substance the same as those of the former enactment, the new enactment shall not be held to operate as new law, but shall be construed and have effect as a consolidation and as declaratory of the law as contained in the former enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(f) (src:426)
GIVEN `the provision is in substance the same as the former provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How a provision of the new enactment is read`
`the new enactment's provision is read, if` `the provision is in substance the same as the former provision` MEANS
    IF   `the provision is in substance the same as the former provision`
    THEN `as a consolidation and as declaratory of the law in the former enactment`
    ELSE `as capable of operating as new law, to the extent that it is not in substance the same`

-- (g) all regulations made under the repealed enactment remain in force and are deemed to have been made under the new enactment,
-- in so far as they are not inconsistent with the new enactment, until they are repealed or others made in their stead.
-- src:427 | (g) all regulations made under the repealed enactment remain in force and are deemed to have been made under the new enactment, in so far as they are not inconsistent with the new enactment, until they are repealed or others made in their stead; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(g) (src:427)
GIVEN `it is inconsistent with the new enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been repealed or others have been made in its stead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a regulation made under the repealed enactment remains in force as made under the new enactment if` `it is inconsistent with the new enactment` `and` `it has been repealed or others have been made in its stead` MEANS
    IF   `it is inconsistent with the new enactment`
    THEN `section 44(g) saves the regulations that are not inconsistent and does not say what becomes of one that is`
    ELSE NOT `it has been repealed or others have been made in its stead`

-- src:427 | (g) all regulations made under the repealed enactment remain in force and are deemed to have been made under the new enactment, in so far as they are not inconsistent with the new enactment, until they are repealed or others made in their stead; and
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(g) (src:427): the inconsistent case is not stated
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(g) saves the regulations that are not inconsistent and does not say what becomes of one that is` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(g) saves the regulations that are not inconsistent and does not say what becomes of one that is"

-- (h) any reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment shall, with respect to a subsequent transaction, matter or
-- thing, be read and construed as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter as the
-- former enactment, but where there are no provisions in the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter, the former
-- enactment shall be read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment.
DECLARE `How a reference to the former enactment is read` IS ONE OF
    `as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment on the same subject-matter`
    `as a reference to the former enactment read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment`

-- src:428 | (h) any reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment shall, with respect to a subsequent transaction, matter or thing, be read and construed as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter as the former enactment, but where there are no provisions in the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter, the former enactment shall be read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(h) (src:428)
GIVEN `the transaction, matter or thing is subsequent to the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new enactment has provisions on the same subject-matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How a reference to the former enactment is read`
`a reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment is read, where` `the transaction, matter or thing is subsequent to the repeal` `and` `the new enactment has provisions on the same subject-matter` MEANS
    IF   `the transaction, matter or thing is subsequent to the repeal`
    THEN IF   `the new enactment has provisions on the same subject-matter`
         THEN `as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment on the same subject-matter`
         ELSE `as a reference to the former enactment read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment`
    ELSE `section 44(h) speaks of a subsequent transaction, matter or thing and does not say how a reference is read for an earlier one`

-- src:428 | (h) any reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment shall, with respect to a subsequent transaction, matter or thing, be read and construed as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter as the former enactment, but where there are no provisions in the new enactment relating to the same subject-matter, the former enactment shall be read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 44(h) (src:428): an earlier transaction is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 44(h) speaks of a subsequent transaction, matter or thing and does not say how a reference is read for an earlier one` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 44(h) speaks of a subsequent transaction, matter or thing and does not say how a reference is read for an earlier one"

§ `Section 46: demise of the Crown`

DECLARE `A thing a demise of the Crown is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `the holding of an office under the Crown in right of Canada`
    `the need for the holder of such an office to be appointed again`
    `the need for the holder of such an office to take again an oath of office or allegiance already taken before the demise`
    `a writ, action or other process or proceeding, civil or criminal, in or issuing out of a court established by an Act`
    `anything else`

-- src:440 | 46 (1) Where there is a demise of the Crown,
-- src:441 | (a) the demise does not affect the holding of any office under the Crown in right of Canada; and
-- src:442 | (b) it is not necessary by reason of the demise that the holder of any such office again be appointed thereto or, having taken an oath of office or allegiance before the demise, again take that oath.
-- src:443 | Continuation of proceedings
-- src:444 | (2) No writ, action or other process or proceeding, civil or criminal, in or issuing out of any court established by an Act is, by reason of a demise of the Crown, determined, abated, discontinued or affected, but every such writ, action, process or proceeding remains in full force and may be enforced, carried on or otherwise proceeded with or completed as though there had been no such demise.
@ref Interpretation Act s 46 (src:440-444)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing a demise of the Crown is asked about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a demise of the Crown affects` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the holding of an office under the Crown in right of Canada` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the need for the holder of such an office to be appointed again` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the need for the holder of such an office to take again an oath of office or allegiance already taken before the demise` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a writ, action or other process or proceeding, civil or criminal, in or issuing out of a court established by an Act` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anything else` THEN `section 46 names offices, oaths and court proceedings and does not say what a demise of the Crown does to anything else`

-- src:440 | 46 (1) Where there is a demise of the Crown,
-- src:441 | (a) the demise does not affect the holding of any office under the Crown in right of Canada; and
-- src:442 | (b) it is not necessary by reason of the demise that the holder of any such office again be appointed thereto or, having taken an oath of office or allegiance before the demise, again take that oath.
-- src:443 | Continuation of proceedings
-- src:444 | (2) No writ, action or other process or proceeding, civil or criminal, in or issuing out of any court established by an Act is, by reason of a demise of the Crown, determined, abated, discontinued or affected, but every such writ, action, process or proceeding remains in full force and may be enforced, carried on or otherwise proceeded with or completed as though there had been no such demise.
@ref Interpretation Act s 46 (src:440-444): nothing else is named
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 46 names offices, oaths and court proceedings and does not say what a demise of the Crown does to anything else` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 46 names offices, oaths and court proceedings and does not say what a demise of the Crown does to anything else"
